  {
    "episode_id": 88428,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88428.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "You know, something that's been also really disheartening to watch is Congress like kind of never acknowledging that the economic suffering that is happening right now is really devastating people's lives in a, you know, not in some abstract way, but in a very real day to day way. And we keep seeing these, you know, rescue these economic rescue bills being discussed and some of them are coming in quickly and some of them are not coming quickly enough. And there is not really, to me at least seems like a vision for something that is more ambitious than just putting a Band-Aid. on the situation and here you have proposed this paycheck guarantee act that is actually very ambitious. Can you talk a little bit about that and also do you think that a big ambitious bill actually has a chance of getting passed in the Congress that we're in right now?",
