    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "You know, the one thing I will say about that is I was really surprised. It's a bipartisan bill. And it's also across the caucus. I got a lot of Democrats who are more conservative and swing districts signed on to it because it's a jobs bill. It's a bill about how you keep people in their jobs. And it also is a pro-business bill because it keeps Business is going to the point where they don't have to deal with shuttering in the midst of a crisis. They get a little bit of relief to stay and figure out what they need to do. It's not going to protect them forever, but it sort of helps them to have time to make these decisions.",
